{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WxwU71tw1KTXcBNrneUqbY","type":"tool_result","content":"ok   corner ledger holds over 10 min (sold 332, $3430)\nok   a shutdown freezes sales\nFAIL a pursuit bot catches Corey (26.9 s, state lost): lost at 26.9\nok   no errors overall\n1 check(s) failed","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c954ed14-e406-494c-b7ce-2e71ce3da87b","uuid":"b56cb942-5ca6-4da0-b0a3-b0a172432943","timestamp":"2026-11-03T21:54:08.568Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"ok   corner ledger holds over 10 min (sold 332, $3430)\nok   a shutdown freezes sales\nFAIL a pursuit bot catches Corey (26.9 s, state lost): lost at 26.9\nok   no errors overall\n1 check(s) failed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/.gitignore","hunks":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":3,"newStart":3,"newLines":6,"lines":[" *:Zone.Identifier"," runs/.smoke.json"," runs/.stop","+runs/.session.json","+runs/.session.json.tmp","+runs/.batches/"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":19,"oldLines":7,"newStart":19,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **CLIs** — what this machine can run. The **CLIs** card shows which CLIs are installed (version, with an **update** button for Claude Code, Codex, Grok and agy that runs the CLI's own `update`; it's off while a batch or test runs, and Muse is updated by hand), the models each offers (click one to add it) and the global instruction files each loads. **Models**: one dropdown per row picks the model (Claude 5.5 family, GPT-6+ on Codex, Grok 4.7, Gemini 3.8 Flash and Gemini 4 Argon on agy, Muse Spark 1.3 and Muse Wonder 1.0; the list is `CATALOG` in `dashboard.html`, and Codex adds any newer GPT-6+ model it lists; only the newest of each GPT line is offered, e.g. gpt-6.1-sol and not gpt-6-sol), which sets the CLI, model ID and run name. **Custom** (bottom of that list, one per CLI) gives a box to type any model ID. Each effort level is its own dropdown holding only the levels that model takes (\"+ effort\" adds another to sweep; Claude Code also offers each level with Ultracode). Then an optional time limit, and **Test**: one tiny task through the real command line and parser, about a minute, to check install, login, model ID, flags and that results are read. Tick \"Test with /goal\" to test the goal loop too. 1-shot runs sweep these models at the efforts set here; the stages in Setup · Advanced pick from them at any effort they take. **CLI commands and flags** holds each CLI's executable and the extra flags added to every run of it."," - **Setup · Basic** — the 1-shot prompt: dimensions and their variants (**Bulk add…** takes a pasted list, one per line, e.g. 100 games for `{{source}}`: each line's text becomes a variant with a short name made from it, or write `short | text`; numbering, bullets and lines already there are skipped, and a text that ran before gets its short name back; **+ Add…** offers your **pinned** variants for the field, then the variants finished runs used that the dimension doesn't have now, labelled as in Results' filters; picking one adds it with its name and text, and a text that ran keeps that name, so its runs count for it. Each variant multiplies the runs, so they're offered, not added. Pin the ones you use often with **pin** on a variant's row, or any of the field's in **+ Add… → Pin or unpin…**; pins are saved in the config as `pinned` (`{ \"genre\": [{ \"id\", \"text\" }] }`), and a config without them starts from `DEFAULT_PINS` in `dashboard.html`: \"use the source\", \"your choice\" and, for perspective, art and animation, \"use the engine\", plus off switches like no goal), the prompt and the file it's saved to. **Prompt history** lists the prompt's versions (v1, v2 …): when each was last edited and first ran, what changed from the one before (fields added or removed, lines), how many runs used it, and buttons to view it or see the changes. A version gets its number when a batch first runs it, so all the edits between two batches make one version; until then it shows on top as the next run's version, saved edits or not. Ctrl+S saves. Errors (like a `{{placeholder}}` with no dimension) block saving; warnings flag efforts or models a CLI won't take and CLIs that aren't installed."," - **Setup · Advanced** — multistage runs: the stages (plan, build, content…) that hand the work from one model or lab to the next, which models and efforts run each, what each is told and when it's done. **Who runs each stage** spells it out: each stage's models, how many sessions it makes per brief and every path a brief takes. See Runs in stages.","-- **Run** — **Basic · 1-shot** or **Advanced · multistage** (when there are stages). In Basic, tick the model+effort pairs and variants you want; in Advanced, pick models per stage (see Runs in stages). **Preview** shows the sample prompt and the batch as terminal sessions: each run's folder (for a later stage, a copy of the one it continues from) and the exact CLI command with what it's sent. The count updates live and skips runs already finished (and says how many of those were made with an older prompt or a variant's old text). Each model shows whether it works (passed a test or has finished runs). Runs take turns across CLIs, so parallel slots go to different services, and start at least 3 seconds apart (see Run folder names); **Max per CLI** caps one CLI to stay inside its plan's rate limits. Preview shows the exact prompt. Start / Stop, with a live log. While a batch runs, **+ Queue** adds another beside it (see Queued batches). **Once a run starts, its model, effort, prompt and time limit are fixed and it runs to the end; nothing running is ended unless you confirm it.** **While a batch runs, Options act on the runs not started yet** (Repeat is fixed once it starts), and every change asks first: **Parallel runs** and **Max per CLI** go up or down, and lowering one below what's running asks whether to let the extra runs finish (no new one starts until there's room) or to end the newest and start them over later; a new **time limit** asks whether it's for runs that start from now or the running ones too (counted from when each started; one already past it ends as timed out); a new **budget** shows what's been spent and what the change does first, and raising a spent one lets runs start again (spend is counted as each run finishes, when the CLI reports it, so the budget never stops a run that's going and one can take it past the budget; a run ended early isn't counted, though it spent); **Retry failed** turned on queues the failed runs skipped earlier, and so does **Resume failed** for the ones it can resume (see Resuming failed runs). **Pause** holds the queue: the running ones finish, or end them to start over when you resume. Each running run has ↻ (end it now, start it over later in this batch) and ✕ (end it now, leave it for the next batch), and each CLI's tally has **skip rest** to leave its queued runs out of this batch. A running agent can't be frozen and picked up where it left off (its time, tokens and cost would then describe two sessions), so an ended run always starts over (a resumed one is resumed again instead); every choice that ends one says so, in red. **Stop** offers Pause first, and Ctrl-C in the dashboard's terminal asks to be pressed again while agents are running. While a batch runs, **Live** shows progress and roughly how long is left, a tally per CLI, each active run against its usual time, and warnings: a CLI whose last 3+ runs failed or that fails most of its runs (with the likely cause), a run going 2× longer than usual for its setup, and finished runs that look off. The header pill and the browser tab's title carry the progress and ⚠ too. A CLI that isn't installed has its runs skipped (not failed).","+- **Run** — **Basic · 1-shot** or **Advanced · multistage** (when there are stages). In Basic, tick the model+effort pairs and variants you want; in Advanced, pick models per stage (see Runs in stages). **Preview** shows the sample prompt and the batch as terminal sessions: each run's folder (for a later stage, a copy of the one it continues from) and the exact CLI command with what it's sent. The count updates live and skips runs already finished (and says how many of those were made with an older prompt or a variant's old text). Each model shows whether it works (passed a test or has finished runs). Runs take turns across CLIs, so parallel slots go to different services, and start at least 3 seconds apart (see Run folder names); **Max per CLI** caps one CLI to stay inside its plan's rate limits. Preview shows the exact prompt. Start / Stop, with a live log. While a batch runs, **+ Queue** adds another beside it (see Queued batches). **Once a run starts, its model, effort, prompt and time limit are fixed and it runs to the end; nothing running is ended unless you confirm it.** **While a batch runs, Options act on the runs not started yet** (Repeat is fixed once it starts), and every change asks first: **Parallel runs** and **Max per CLI** go up or down, and lowering one below what's running asks whether to let the extra runs finish (no new one starts until there's room) or to end the newest and start them over later; a new **time limit** asks whether it's for runs that start from now or the running ones too (counted from when each started; one already past it ends as timed out); a new **budget** shows what's been spent and what the change does first, and raising a spent one lets runs start again (spend is counted as each run finishes, when the CLI reports it, so the budget never stops a run that's going and one can take it past the budget; a run ended early isn't counted, though it spent); **Retry failed** turned on queues the failed runs skipped earlier, and so does **Resume failed** for the ones it can resume (see Resuming failed runs). **Pause** holds the queue: the running ones finish, or end them to start over when you resume. Each running run has ↻ (end it now, start it over later in this batch) and ✕ (end it now, leave it for the next batch), and each CLI's tally has **skip rest** to leave its queued runs out of this batch. A running agent can't be frozen and picked up where it left off (its time, tokens and cost would then describe two sessions), so a run ended here always starts over (a resumed one is resumed again instead); every choice that ends one says so, in red. **Stop** offers Pause first. Quitting or restarting the dashboard is different: the batch is kept to pick up, and a Claude Code session it cuts off carries on where it was (see Restarting the dashboard); Ctrl-C in the dashboard's terminal asks to be pressed again while agents are running. While a batch runs, **Live** shows progress and roughly how long is left, a tally per CLI, each active run against its usual time, and warnings: a CLI whose last 3+ runs failed or that fails most of its runs (with the likely cause), a run going 2× longer than usual for its setup, and finished runs that look off. The header pill and the browser tab's title carry the progress and ⚠ too. A CLI that isn't installed has its runs skipped (not failed)."," - **Results** — filter by anything (including CLI and prompt version; on phones the filters fold behind a button, and each run is a card). **Compare** shows how B differs from A on any field: model + effort (opus · medium → sonnet · medium), effort (medium → high), a variant, CLI or prompt version, optionally **for each** value of another field. Effort medium → high for each model shows which model gains more from extra effort. **Only matching variants** pairs runs that differ only in what's compared; a change in bold goes the same way in at least 80% of 3+ pairs. **Averages by group** gives plain averages (time, cost, list price, output tokens, score, delivered %). Each run's **list $** is its tokens at the labs' public API prices (see What each CLI reports), so it compares across CLIs; its details add model requests, tool calls, compactions, subagents and the plan's usage. ⚑ marks a flagged run (see Insights), ⟳ a resumed one and \"resumable\" a failed one Resume failed can carry on with (filter or compare by **resumed**). ▶ plays the game, details shows everything about a run, reply shows the agent's Source Information and feedback, interview its exit interview (`exit-interview.json`, see The record in each game), failed runs show why, `out` shows the raw CLI output. Score out of 10 and add notes while you play. Variant columns that are the same for every run shown are named once above the table instead of on every row."," - **Insights** — what the runs say without playing them all. Filter by time (all, last 24 hours, last 7 days, last batch) and any field.","   - **Expectations** checks what should hold: more effort brings more output and time (same model, matching variants), finished runs leave a game file, a final reply and the exit interview their prompt asks for, no TODO/FIXME left, repeats of a setup agree, one prompt version, and each CLI on one version."]},{"oldStart":90,"oldLines":6,"newStart":90,"newLines":14,"lines":[" - **Live** lists the batches and how far each is; **take out** leaves out the runs one hasn't started (its running ones finish; they run next time). **Stop** stops them all. The budget counts what all of them spend."," - Runs are matched by short name, so to run a variant's new text beside a queued batch that has its old text, give the variant a new short name."," ","+## Restarting the dashboard","+**⟳ Restart dashboard** (Run → Live) starts the dashboard again with its code as it is now (`dashboard.mjs`, `run-matrix.mjs` and the page, which reloads itself once it's back; with unsaved edits or a dialog open it asks first), so a change to them takes effect without losing the batch. `node dashboard.mjs` keeps the dashboard in a child process of its own for this and starts it again when it asks.","+- **A batch going picks up where it left off by itself** once it's back, in a few seconds: the same batches with their settings (Pause too), log, spend and copies of Setup and the prompt. Its runners skip what's done, carry on what was cut off and start the rest.","+- **Runs going are cut off.** A Claude Code session that has had its first answer carries on where it was (`claude -p --resume`, sent its `/goal` again or \"continue where you left off\"), work folder and all; only the request it was waiting on is asked again. A run of another CLI, or one that hadn't had an answer yet, starts over, and Restart says which before you confirm. With runs going it offers **Restart once they have finished** instead: no new runs start meanwhile, so nothing is cut off (**Restart now** or **Call it off** while it waits).","+- **Quit (Ctrl-C) cuts them off the same way**, but the dashboard doesn't come back by itself. The next time it starts, the Run tab offers the batch under **Pick up where you left off** (what's finished, what's left, which cut-off runs carry on and which start over), with **Resume the batch** and **Forget it**. So it does after a crash or the computer going down: the session is saved as it changes (`runs/.session.json`), and an agent still going after its runner was killed outright (nobody can hear it any more) is ended before its session carries on (Linux).","+- **A cut-off run carries on whenever a batch has it**, Resume failed or not; Forget it doesn't change that, and Start or Preview count it. Until then it isn't a result (Results, Insights and the report don't count it): its folder holds `unfinished.json`. A run still going in another runner is left out of a batch.","+- **What's recorded:** a cut-off run that carries on is one run, like a resumed one: ⟳ in Results, its sessions in `parts` (the cut-off one has `cutOff`), its time, tokens and cost added up. A session cut off never printed its totals, so its tokens are its responses' in its transcript (`~/.claude/projects`) and its cost is those at list price, which is what Claude Code reports too (`costSource: estimated`); if Claude Code saved the session's totals as it stopped (a `cost-state`), those count instead. Ended mid-way (Stop, ↻, ✕) as it carries on, it stays cut off and carries on again next time.","+"," ## The record in each game"," Once a run ends, its record goes into the game file itself, so a game passed around (or put on ai-hub) says what made it, what it took and what the agent said about it, including what's only known at the end: time, tokens, cost. It's enough to rebuild the run's place in the dashboard from the game alone (see Reading them back). It's an inert `<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"cc-matrix-run\">` block just before `</body>`: read it in a page with `JSON.parse(document.getElementById('cc-matrix-run').textContent)`, or anywhere with `run-record.mjs` (no dependencies: `readRecord()`, or the commands below). Schema 2; `run-record.schema.json` has every field."," "]},{"oldStart":120,"oldLines":7,"newStart":128,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - `matrix.config.json` — everything the CLIs and Setup tabs edit (hand-editable too)"," - `run-record.mjs` — the record in each game: writes it (for `run-matrix.mjs`), reads it, `export` and `rebuild` (see The record in each game); `run-record.schema.json` describes it"," - `prompt-template.md` — the prompt's headings, with each section's `{{name}}` (see The prompt is its sections); every run also fills `{{model}}`, `{{effort}}` (with `-ultracode` when on), `{{lab}}`, `{{environment}}` (CLI and OS), `{{stamp}}` (when the run started, to the second: `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS` in the computer's time zone, e.g. `20261029-075312`; the same everywhere in one run, so it ties the game's file name to its run) and `{{date}}` (that moment as `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS`)","-- `runs/<run-id>/` — `work/` (the game; the bundled .html in its root, with the agent's `exit-interview.json` beside it), `prompt.md`, `reply.md`, `result.json`, `agent.out` (everything the CLI printed: for Claude Code, Grok and agy the whole event stream, a few MB for a long run), `agent.err`; a resumed run has each later session's as `agent.2.out`, `agent.2.err` and so on","+- `runs/<run-id>/` — `work/` (the game; the bundled .html in its root, with the agent's `exit-interview.json` beside it), `prompt.md`, `reply.md`, `result.json`, `agent.out` (everything the CLI printed: for Claude Code, Grok and agy the whole event stream, a few MB for a long run), `agent.err`; a resumed run has each later session's as `agent.2.out`, `agent.2.err` and so on. `unfinished.json` while the run's agent works, and after, in a run that was cut off (see Restarting the dashboard)","+- `runs/.session.json`, `runs/.batches/` — the batch going (or cut off) and each batch's copy of the config and prompt, kept until it ends, so it can be picked up after a restart or quit (not committed)"," - `runs/prompt-history.json` — every version of the prompt a batch has run: its number, hash, when it was last edited (`at`) and first ran (`ranAt`), and its text (Setup → Prompt history)"," - `runs/scores.json` — your scores, notes and \"looked at\" marks, each saved with the run's `startedAt`: a re-run starts unreviewed, and deleting a run deletes its review. `runs/.smoke.json` — the latest Test result per model"," - `runs/results.csv` — everything in one spreadsheet; `runs/index.html` is a static gallery"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/dashboard.html","hunks":[{"oldStart":1485,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1485,"newLines":11,"lines":[" }"," "," // -------------------------------------------------------------------- RUN","+// Runs cut off mid-way (the dashboard quit or restarted, the computer went down; the server lists them as status.cut):","+// never done, and the next batch that has one carries on with its session where it was (on: a Claude Code session","+// that had got going) or starts it over.","+const cutKeys = () => cached('cutKeys', () => { const cut = status.cut ?? [];","+  return { all: new Set(cut.map(runKey)), on: new Set(cut.filter((c) => c.carriesOn).map(runKey)) }; });"," // Mirrors run-matrix.mjs: a finished run counts for the id it would get now. One from before a dimension"," // was added counts as that dimension's olderRuns variant (else its first); a dimension removed since is left out."," const olderVariant = (d) => (cfg.dimensions[d].find((v) => v.olderRuns) ?? cfg.dimensions[d][0])?.id;"]},{"oldStart":1513,"oldLines":10,"newStart":1518,"newLines":11,"lines":["   const count = pick.length * combos * repeat;","   let done = 0, doneOld = 0, resume = 0; // doneOld: of those, made with an older prompt or a variant's old text","   if (count <= 50000) {","-    // Resume failed: failed runs that got partway carry on with their session (the server says which can).","-    const resumable = (r) => r.status !== 'ok' && r.resumable && resumeOn();","-    const doneRuns = new Map(results.filter((r) => r.status === 'ok' || !(sel.opts.rerunFailed || resumable(r))).map((r) => [runKey(r), r]));","-    const resumes = new Set(results.filter(resumable).map(runKey));","+    // Resume failed: failed runs that got partway carry on with their session (the server says which can), and so do","+    // runs cut off mid-way whose session had got going, whatever the options (cutKeys).","+    const resumable = (r) => r.status !== 'ok' && r.resumable && resumeOn(), cut = cutKeys();","+    const doneRuns = new Map(results.filter((r) => r.status === 'ok' || (!cut.all.has(runKey(r)) && !(sel.opts.rerunFailed || resumable(r)))).map((r) => [runKey(r), r]));","+    const resumes = new Set([...results.filter(resumable).map(runKey), ...cut.on]);","     const walk = (i, acc, base) => {","       if (i === lists.length) {","         for (let r = 1; r <= repeat; r++) {"]},{"oldStart":1550,"oldLines":9,"newStart":1556,"newLines":9,"lines":["       const k = `${briefKeyOf(r)}|${chainKey(r.chain.slice(0, -1))}|${r.chain.at(-1).stage}`;","       (have.get(k) ?? have.set(k, []).get(k)).push(r.chain);","     }","-    const resumable = (r) => r.status !== 'ok' && r.resumable && resumeOn();","-    const doneRuns = new Set(results.filter((r) => r.chain && (r.status === 'ok' || !(sel.opts.rerunFailed || resumable(r)))).map(runKey));","-    const resumes = new Set(results.filter((r) => r.chain && resumable(r)).map(runKey));","+    const resumable = (r) => r.status !== 'ok' && r.resumable && resumeOn(), cut = cutKeys();","+    const doneRuns = new Set(results.filter((r) => r.chain && (r.status === 'ok' || (!cut.all.has(runKey(r)) && !(sel.opts.rerunFailed || resumable(r))))).map(runKey));","+    const resumes = new Set([...results.filter((r) => r.chain && resumable(r)).map(runKey), ...cut.on]);","     const walk = (i, acc) => {","       if (i < lists.length) { for (const v of lists[i]) walk(i + 1, [...acc, v]); return; }","       const bk = acc.join('__');"]},{"oldStart":1689,"oldLines":8,"newStart":1695,"newLines":9,"lines":["       d === GOAL_DIM && vs.some((v) => (v.text || '').trim()) ? h('p', { class: 'hint', style: 'margin:8px 0 0' }, '* Not on Codex: it has no headless /goal, so it gets the same prompt without /goal.') : null);","   }));"," ","-  // While a batch runs, Live comes right after the summary, so it's on screen without scrolling.","-  morph($('#tab-run'), summary, running ? liveCard() : null, models, dims, running ? null : liveCard());","+  // While a batch runs, Live comes right after the summary, so it's on screen without scrolling. A batch cut off before","+  // (the dashboard quit or restarted) is offered first, to pick up.","+  morph($('#tab-run'), restartedBanner(), !running && status.saved ? savedCard() : null, summary, running ? liveCard() : null, models, dims, running ? null : liveCard());","   const pre = $('#logpre'); if (pre && logFollow) pre.scrollTop = pre.scrollHeight;"," }"," "]},{"oldStart":1730,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1737,"newLines":14,"lines":["     : st.finishedAt ? `Last batch ended ${new Date(st.finishedAt).toLocaleString()} (${st.finished} finished)` : 'No batch started since the dashboard opened.';","   // A running batch takes changes (see adjust): each run can be ended, to start over later or to leave out.","   const ctl = st.running && st.state && !st.stopping;","-  return h('div', { class: 'card', id: 'live', key: 'live' }, h('h2', {}, 'Live'), h('p', { class: 'sub' }, head),","+  const now = restartingNow || st.restarting === 'now';","+  return h('div', { class: 'card', id: 'live', key: 'live' },","+    h('div', { class: 'row' }, h('h2', { class: 'grow' }, 'Live'),","+      meta.canRestart ? h('button', { class: 'btn', onclick: restartDashboard, disabled: now || !!st.updating || (st.stopping && !st.restarting),","+        title: 'Start the dashboard again with its code as it is now; a batch going picks up where it left off' }, now ? 'Restarting…' : '⟳ Restart dashboard') : null),","+    h('p', { class: 'sub' }, head),","+    now ? h('p', { class: 'warns', style: 'margin:0 0 10px' }, '⟳ Restarting the dashboard: this page reloads itself when it\\'s back, in a few seconds'","+      + (st.running ? '. The batch then picks up where it left off.' : '.')) : null,","     st.running ? holding() : null,","     (st.batches?.length ?? 0) > 1 ? queueList(st, ctl) : null,","     hb ? liveHealth(hb) : null,"]},{"oldStart":1839,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1853,"newLines":9,"lines":["   const resumes = s.resume ? ` (${s.resume} of them resume their session where it stopped)` : '';","   const order = staged ? `\\n\\nIn stages: ${Object.entries(s.stages).map(([st, p]) => `${st} (${p.length} model${p.length === 1 ? '' : 's'})`).join(' → ')}. `","     + 'A run starts once the run it continues from has finished OK; if that one fails, the runs after it are left for the next batch.' : '';","-  if (!confirm(`Start ${n} run${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}${resumes}, ${sel.opts.concurrency || 1} at a time${budget}?${order}\\n\\nAgents run with permission prompts off.${note}\\n\\n`","+  const forgets = status.saved ? '\\n\\nThe batch cut off before (Pick up where you left off, above) is forgotten: Resume it instead to run it as it was started. '","+    + 'Its cut-off runs still carry on whenever a batch has them.' : '';","+  if (!confirm(`Start ${n} run${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}${resumes}, ${sel.opts.concurrency || 1} at a time${budget}?${order}${forgets}\\n\\nAgents run with permission prompts off.${note}\\n\\n`","     + `Once a run starts, its model, effort, prompt and time limit are fixed and it runs to the end. While the batch runs you can still change `","     + `Parallel runs, Max per CLI, Budget, Time limit and Retry failed, and pause it: changes apply to the runs not started yet. `","     + `Nothing that's running is ended unless you confirm it.`)) return;"]},{"oldStart":1990,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2006,"newLines":9,"lines":["   if (active.length) {","     const k = active.length;","     const how = await choose('Pause the batch', [`No new runs start until you resume. ${k === 1 ? '1 run is' : `${k} runs are`} going now.`,","-      'A running agent can\\'t be frozen and picked up later where it left off, so pausing lets it finish unless you choose to end it.'],","+      'A running agent can\\'t be frozen and picked up later where it left off, so pausing lets it finish unless you choose to end it.',","+      meta.canRestart ? 'Pausing to restart the dashboard (to load its latest code)? Use ⟳ Restart dashboard instead: it can wait for the runs going to finish, '","+        + 'and the batch carries on by itself once it\\'s back.' : null],","       [{ value: 'finish', primary: true, label: 'Let the running ones finish', hint: 'Nothing is lost; the batch waits for you once they\\'re done.' },","        { value: 'requeue', danger: true, label: `End ${k === 1 ? 'it' : `all ${k}`} now and start ${k === 1 ? 'it' : 'them'} over when you resume`, hint: lo